--- 3. re-calibrate on all days so far
# Calibration report (2026-09-27)

3317 rows, 364 tokens, 5 day(s) (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-27). Target: cost of selling immediately across all measured venues, vs consolidated mid. 5-fold CV grouped by token.
2750 more sales could not be absorbed by the merged book at all (no venue truncated). They can't be fitted, so they're scored instead: 'false comfort' = share a model prices under 10%. Dropped: 569 sales where a venue capped its levels (thin vs truncated unknowable); 0 token-days with no CMC volume/sigma.

| model | Y | delta | median abs err | median factor off | R^2 (log) | false comfort |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| textbook sqrt, global Y **(shipped)** | 1.7 | 0.500 | 13.8 bps | x1.80 | 0.491 | 81% |
| power law, global Y | 7.53 | 0.720 | 15.3 bps | x1.78 | 0.542 | 46% |
| learned Y per token | per token | 0.720 | 14.0 bps | x1.69 | 0.615 | 47% |

Median absolute error by order size (out-of-fold, bps):

| size | n | sqrt | power | learned |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| $10,000 | 1490 | 8.5 | 8.3 | 6.8 |
| $100,000 | 1310 | 25.0 | 33.3 | 29.0 |
| $1,000,000 | 417 | 22.8 | 33.3 | 33.7 |
| $10,000,000 | 100 | 96.9 | 96.7 | 86.7 |

What predicts a token's Y (GBM feature importance): log_sigma 0.47, history_days 0.18, turnover 0.15, log_mcap 0.11, log_volume 0.09

The learned model did not beat the power law by the required 5%, so the power law ships. Published as a negative result.

Wrote ingest/calibration.json (used by impact.py) and data/calibration_report.md (for METHODOLOGY.md).
